[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C code actually distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Runtime options / modes / flags:** *none.* `c_src/include/driver.h` exposes a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m single entry point with no flag, mode, enum or context parameter:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void driver(const char *s1, const char *s2);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `grep` over `c_src/` finds no `if`, `switch`, `#ifdef` (other than the header's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m include guard), no global/static state, and no setter — so there is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m configuration to toggle. `translation/Cargo.toml` likewise defines no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `[features]`, so there is no compile-time axis either.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Public entry points:** `driver` is both the highest- and the lowest-level entry
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m point; there is no convenience wrapper hiding a lower-level API. The one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *internal* routine the C composes is libc `strcspn`, which the Rust reimplements
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m by hand — that reimplementation is the real subject of these tests, and it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m driven through the exported `driver` symbol exactly as an external caller would.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Input shapes the code special-cases:** the branching all lives inside
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `strcspn`'s scan, whose behaviour is a function of (length of `s1`, length of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `s2`, position of the first byte of `s1` that is a member of `s2`, and whether
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m such a byte exists at all), plus `printf("%zu\n", ...)`'s rendering of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m resulting `size_t`. glibc's `strcspn` additionally switches between a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bitmap/SIMD path and a scalar path on the size of the reject set, so reject-set
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m size is a real axis even though the visible C has no branch on it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axes, enumerated:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `len(s1)`: 0 · 1 · small (2–8) · medium (9–64) · large (crosses vector-width
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and page boundaries) · huge (1 MiB)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `len(s2)`: 0 · 1 · small · medium · 255 (every non-NUL byte) · huge
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * match position in `s1`: none · first byte · interior · last byte
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * byte alphabet: ASCII printable · full `0x01`–`0xFF` (exercises the signed-`char`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   comparison) · single repeated byte
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `s2` содержит duplicates / is a superset of `s1`'s alphabet / is disjoint from it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * pointer placement: `s1` and `s2` aliasing the same buffer; `s1` at a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   non-8-byte-aligned offset (glibc's `strcspn` has alignment-dependent paths)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Rows (cross-product, pruned to combinations the code treats differently)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
